  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "The base length and height of a triangle increase by a factor of 3. By what factor does the area increase?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "A factor of $9$.",
      "worked": "Let the original base and height be $b$ and $h$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{bh}{2}\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=\\frac{(3b)(3h)}{2}\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=9\\frac{bh}{2}\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=9A\\end{align*}$$\nThe area increases by a factor of $9$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
  },
